use /lib
from /scope/project-directory import ProjectDirectoryScope

export scope LSP:
    concept: {LSPConcept}

concept LSPConcept:
    pitch:
        LSP-based autocompleting for the chat input, and language support for
        the editor, will be provided via the `piton lsp`

    shape: {LSPShape}

shape LSPShape:
    description:
        Completions and auto-imports for the Piton typed into the chat input,
        and the server the editor's Piton files are edited with.

    server:
        One `piton lsp` is started as a child process in the selected
        ${ProjectDirectoryScope}, speaking JSON-RPC over stdio, shared by the
        chat input and the editor, and restarted whenever the project
        directory changes. The client sends `initialize` and `initialized`,
        answers any request from the server with an empty result, and gives up
        on a request after 5 seconds. Diagnostics the server publishes are
        kept per file and passed on to whatever shows that file. If the server
        cannot be started, the input and the editor still work, without
        language support.

    document:
        The server never sees the input's text directly. It sees the hidden
        anchor, as an in-memory document at `.suspense-draft.pi` in the
        project's spec root, kept current with `textDocument/didOpen` and
        full-text `textDocument/didChange`. Positions are translated between
        the input and the hidden anchor's `userPrompt` lines, in UTF-16
        columns.

    completion:
        `textDocument/completion` is requested after typing a letter, a
        digit, an opening curly brace, a period, a dollar sign, an at sign,
        a colon, or an underscore. Results are narrowed to what has been
        typed of the current word, matches at the start of a name before
        matches anywhere in it, then ordered by the server's sort text. The
        hidden anchor's own name is never offered. Accepting a completion
        inserts it into the input, and the import the server attaches to it
        (`additionalTextEdits`) is added to the hidden anchor instead of the
        input.

    autoImport:
        Names typed by hand are imported with the server's
        `textDocument/codeAction` quick fixes, repeated up to three times
        since one import can bring more names into reach. This runs before
        each completion request and before a prompt is sent.

    completionPopup:
        The completion popup opens at the cursor and is location-aware: it
        always stays fully inside the window. It opens below the cursor when
        there is room and above it otherwise, which is the usual case since
        the input sits at the bottom of the window. It shifts left rather
        than running past the right edge. Any documentation for the selected
        completion sits beside the list when both fit across the window, and
        is otherwise stacked with the list, on the side away from the
        cursor.
